From 0a26fd22a0494fc1d5a59021243595328ab47178 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joethedev5 <deepsbx1@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 06:05:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Recover the hypervisor trap dispatcher and its headers

Reconstruct osfmk/arm64/hv/hv.c from the kasan reference kernel and
the KDK 27.0.1 DWARF:

 - hv_internal_isa_guest_allowed (line 47) and hv_init (300), which
   parses the "hypervisor" boot arg, sets the flag and returns
   hv_paranested_virtualization_init().
 - _hv_trap_capabilities (338): asserts hv_get_support(), sizes the
   buffer from the shared measurement's capabilities entry (offset
   0xd8), allocates it page-aligned and zeroed with tag
   VM_KERN_MEMORY_HV, fills it with hv_get_host_capabilities(), copies
   min(size, sizeof(hv_capabilities_t)) bytes out and returns
   HV_ERROR/HV_SUCCESS.
 - The 19-entry _vm_trap dispatch table (380) with handlers for
   capabilities, the VM and vCPU traps, and the paravirtualized nested
   service; the recovered handler addresses match the reference table.
 - hv_lck_grp and hv_mtx (405/407).
 - hv_trap (410): reads the trap and argument from saved-state x0/x1,
   emits the KDBG_RELEASE start/end events (MACHDBG_CODE(
   DBG_MACH_EXCP_SC, 5)), dispatches through _vm_trap when
   hv_get_support() is set and writes the result back to x0.
 - The thread and task destroy callbacks (433/439) tail-call
   hv_vcpu_destroy() and hv_vm_destroy().

Complete the headers this needs: the hypervisor error codes in
hv_kern_types.h; new hv_vm.h and hv_vcpu.h with the declarations and
reference line numbers recovered from the DWARF; the compatibility
helper declarations in hv_compat_paranested.h; the packed
hv_capabilities_t and hv_paranested_measurement_t layouts in
hv_interface.h (confirmed by DWARF member offsets and size 475/228);
and the lock/object includes in hv_internal.h, hv_objects.h.

The translation unit compiles with its recovered DW_AT_APPLE_flags and
produces the reference instruction sequences for hv_init, hv_trap and
_hv_trap_capabilities.  The reference's bounds-safety wide pointer in
the copyout path is approximated with a plain vm_offset_t (local clang
lacks bounds-safety), and the trap index names are recorded as comments
because the 13432 TRAP_HV_* definitions are not in the KDK.

Authored-By: joethedev5 <joeshmo@nunya.com>
